lity":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Which single description best fits this opportunity?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Legitimate"},"2":{"Display":"High-risk but legitimate"},"3":{"Display":"Scam \/ fraud-indicative"},"4":{"Display":"Unclear \/ insufficient information to classify"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID23"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_1Y9pogwV6Kgb0Ee","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID24","SecondaryAttribute":"Investment opportunity Investor profile: The investor is considering putting $10,000 into the opp...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<h3>Investment opportunity<\/h3><div><br><\/div><p><b>Investor profile:<\/b> The investor is considering putting $10,000 into the opportunity below. The $10,000 is money they can afford to invest and will not need for at least five years. They already have emergency savings and no high-interest debt.<\/p><p><br><\/p><p><b>Opportunity:<\/b> I\u2019m looking at a listed REIT that owns office buildings in several large US cities. It pays a fairly attractive income, but it also uses quite a lot of debt \u2014 roughly three dollars of debt for every dollar of equity \u2014 and it lost around 60% during one particularly bad market period. The shares are publicly traded and the company regularly reports its property holdings and debt levels.<\/p><p><br><\/p><p>Please evaluate this opportunity using your professional judgment.<\/p>","DataExportTag":"R1_SCENARIO","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Investment opportunity Investor profile: The investor is considering putting $10,000 into the opp...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":1,"NextAnswer